docs/followups/pi-observability-2026-05-21.md:28:## Transition plan for `pi-opik-cli-bridge`
docs/followups/pi-observability-2026-05-21.md:30:The transitional `extensions/observability/pi-opik-cli-bridge.js` ships pi turn data to Opik through a CLI bridge (`~/.local/share/opik-cli-bridge/bridge.js`). It is wired into `my-pi-full` and `my-pi-pod` today. Migration to `pi-observability` proceeds in three stages, none of which require touching the bridge during steps 1\u20132:
docs/followups/pi-observability-2026-05-21.md:33:2. **Soak with dual-lane.** Compare a week of `pi-opik-cli-bridge` vs `pi-observability` Opik traces. Reconcile any divergence (turn IDs, model attribution, deployment env). Acceptance: `pi-observability` traces are a superset of `pi-opik-cli-bridge` traces by turn id.
